  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.217,
            0.149,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 0,
              "bbox": [
                0.113,
                0.217,
                0.149,
                0.243
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_0.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.753,
            0.048,
            0.86,
            0.067
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Algebra Play"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us approach this problem systematically. There are six ways to place three digits:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.132,
            0.57,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can fill the first box with 2, 3 or 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.156,
            0.846,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• For each of these choices, we have 2 ways of filling the remaining 2 digits."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.198,
            0.787,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The six options are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 3 \\times 5 , 2 5 \\times 3 , 3 2 \\times 5 , 3 5 \\times 2 , 5 2 \\times 3 , 5 3 \\times 2 ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.219,
            0.747,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do we find the largest product among these six options?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.245,
            0.748,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can group them in pairs where the multiplier is the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.269,
            0.37,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• 35 × 2 and 53 × 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.293,
            0.372,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• 25 × 3 and 52 × 3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.317,
            0.371,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• 23 × 5 and 32 × 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.341,
            0.846,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In each pair, the one with the larger multiplicand generates the larger product, so we can reduce the comparison to these three expressions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.384,
            0.268,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 3 \\times 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.407,
            0.269,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 2 \\times 3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.431,
            0.268,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 2 \\times 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.456,
            0.845,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is clear that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 2 \\times 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is bigger than 53 × 2, so we only need to compare 52 × 3 and 32 × 5. Let us expand these."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.497,
            0.471,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• 32 × 5 = (3 × 10 × 5) + (2 × 5)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.522,
            0.472,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• 52 × 3 = (5 × 10 × 3) + (2 × 3)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.546,
            0.846,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first terms in both expressions are the same. The second term shows that 32 × 5 is larger, and hence the largest of the six possible products we can form with 2, 3 and 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.605,
            0.846,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ In this case, we used the largest digit as the multiplier. The other two digits were arranged in decreasing order to form the multiplicand. Will this always be the case? Let us find out using algebra."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.666,
            0.707,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose p, q, and r are the three digits such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p < q < r ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.685,
            0.845,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As before, we have six possible products, which we group by the multiplier:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.728,
            0.333,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q r \\times p , \\underline { r } q \\times p"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.752,
            0.332,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "pr \\times q,rp \\times q"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.776,
            0.331,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p q \\times r , q p \\times r"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.8,
            0.845,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In each pair, the multiplicand with the larger tens digit forms the larger product. So we have three products to compare:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.844,
            0.266,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "r q \\times p"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.869,
            0.267,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "r p \\times q"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.892,
            0.267,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q p \\times r"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.869,
            0.913,
            0.918,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "143"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
